      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "SceneRef - Studio\n\n1. SceneRef Resolution: the shape and size the viewer renders the scene at (its camera frame follows).\n2. Viewer: Browse... a .blend or .duf, frame the shot. Mannequins are optional: + Figure marks where a person stands (sitting poses snap onto seats); without any, the action text places people.\n3. Studio > create: image (FLUX.2 Klein, Qwen-Image + ControlNet, Krea2) or movie (MiniMax H3 ref2va, with sound). Only that mode's settings show.\n4. Studio > Cast: + character for each person to recognise (.char / RefMod or + picture). Tying them to a mannequin colour is optional.\n5. action: what happens and how it should look (names as in the cast, clothing too; for a movie, speech in quotes after says / asks). It only guides the prompt writer. Press 'Write the picture prompt' (or movie prompt): the vision model writes the whole prompt into the box below for the chosen model. Edit it, or write your own; the box is exactly what the model gets.\n6. picture_size / picture_aspect (or movie_size / movie_aspect) set the output independently of the viewer; Match camera makes them the viewer's own.\n7. Run. Preview & Save shows the result; in manual mode press 'Save to output' to keep it. Advanced (in the Studio): steps, cfg, sampler, scheduler (filled with the model's defaults), face pass, models.\n\nNo .char yet? The 'SceneRef - Character Maker' workflow makes one from photos."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "SceneRef - Studio\n\n1. SceneRef Resolution: the shape and size the viewer renders the scene at (its camera frame follows).\n2. Viewer: Browse... a .blend or .duf, frame the shot. Mannequins are optional: + Figure marks where a person stands (sitting poses snap onto seats); without any, the action text places people.\n3. Studio > create: image (FLUX.2 Klein, Qwen-Image + ControlNet, Krea2) or movie (MiniMax H3 ref2va, with sound). Only that mode's settings show.\n4. Studio > Cast: + character for each person to recognise (.char / RefMod or + picture). Tying them to a mannequin colour is optional.\n5. action: what happens and how it should look (names as in the cast, clothing too; for a movie, speech in quotes after says / asks). It only guides the prompt writer. Press 'Write the picture prompt' (or movie prompt): the vision model writes the whole prompt into the box below for the chosen model. Edit it, or write your own; the box is exactly what the model gets.\n6. picture_size / picture_aspect (or movie_size / movie_aspect) set the output independently of the viewer; Match camera makes them the viewer's own.\n7. Run. Preview & Save shows the result; in manual mode press 'Save to output' to keep it. Advanced (in the Studio): steps, cfg, sampler, scheduler (filled with the model's defaults), face pass, models.\n\nNo .char yet? The 'SceneRef - Character Maker' workflow makes one from photos."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
